# Installing libambx

`libambx` is the publishable continuation of the original Combustd driver.
The core library needs Ruby 3.1 or newer, libusb available on the system, and
the `libusb` Ruby gem. Install a published release with:

```sh
gem install libambx
```

To develop from this checkout:

```sh
bundle install
bundle exec rake test
```

The original Combustd applications may have their own dependencies; look for
an `INSTALL` file in their respective directories.

Installing these dependencies might be as trivial as using your package manager (apt, aptitude, yum, ports, fink, etc.), if these fail or are missing request them at your maintainer or choose to install them from source.

libusb: http://www.libusb.org/
libusb gem: https://github.com/larskanis/libusb
